              <p>Kitchen and bathroom remodels typically provide a strong return on investment. Adding energy-efficient windows, new flooring, or additional square footage can also make your home more appealing to future buyers. The <a href="https://www.remodeling.hw.net/cost-vs-value/2025/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Remodeling Magazine Cost vs. Value Report</a> shows kitchen remodels recoup 60–80% of their cost at resale — one of the strongest returns of any home improvement. Research from the <a href="https://www.jchs.harvard.edu/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Joint Center for Housing Studies at Harvard University</a> also confirms that renovation spending consistently outpaces new home purchases as a share of total housing investment.</p>
            </div>

